# Testing

> Progressive-disclosure reference for how this project is tested.
{% if primary_language == "python" %}
## Running tests
- All: `uv run pytest`
- Single test: `uv run pytest tests/test_<name>.py`
- Focused run: `uv run pytest tests/test_<name>.py::test_<case>`
{% elif primary_language == "typescript" %}
## Running tests
- All: `npm test`
- Single test: `npx vitest run <path>`
{% elif primary_language == "rust" %}
## Running tests
- All: `cargo test`
- Single test: `cargo test <test_name>`
{% elif primary_language == "go" %}
## Running tests
- All: `go test ./...`
- Single test: `go test ./... -run <TestName>`
{% else %}
## Running tests
- (Fill in the test commands for this stack.)
{% endif %}

## Conventions
- Tests live under `tests/` mirroring the source layout.
- Prefer behavior-focused tests over implementation details.
- Keep tests fast and deterministic; avoid network calls in unit tests.
